    <h2 id="si_visual_title">Work where the website happens.</h2>
    <p>Select an element on the page and adjust it in place. Shape the layout, edit the content, and see how the pieces fit together as you work.</p>
    <figure class="si-workspace" aria-label="An illustration of a page built from reusable blocks">
      <figcaption><span><i class="si-status-dot" aria-hidden="true"></i> YOUR WORKSPACE</span><span>PAGE / HOME</span></figcaption>
      <div class="si-workspace-body">
        <div class="si-outline"><span class="si-demo-label">PAGE STRUCTURE</span><div><span aria-hidden="true">▾</span> Home</div><ul><li>Header</li><li class="si-outline-selected">Introduction <span>↗</span></li><li>Features</li><li>Footer</li></ul><span class="si-outline-hint">Four blocks. One page.</span></div>
        <div class="si-demo-canvas"><span class="si-demo-label">INTRODUCTION</span><div class="si-demo-selection"><span class="si-selection-label">Heading</span><p>Your next idea<br>starts here<span>.</span></p><span class="si-selection-handle" aria-hidden="true"></span></div><p class="si-demo-caption">A little structure. A lot of possibility.</p><span class="si-demo-link">Make it yours <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></span></div>
      </div>
      <div class="si-workspace-footer"><span>Structure you can see.</span><span>Details you can change.</span></div>
    </figure>
  </section>

  <section id="reusable-blocks" class="si-chapter" aria-labelledby="si_blocks_title">
    <p class="si-eyebrow">03 / REUSABLE BLOCKS</p>
    <h2 id="si_blocks_title">A few good pieces go a long way.</h2>
    <p>Build with sections you can understand and reuse. A header, a navigation menu, a content area, a footer: each block has its own markup, styles, and behavior.</p>
    <div class="si-table-wrap" role="region" aria-label="The building blocks of a website" tabindex="0">
      <table><thead><tr><th scope="col">Building block</th><th scope="col">What it does</th></tr></thead><tbody>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>Pages</code></th><td>Give each destination a name, a path, and a place in your site.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>Blocks</code></th><td>Organize the sections that make up a page, and reuse them across the site.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>Styles</code></th><td>Control how each element looks, from type and color to spacing and layout.</td></tr>
        <tr><th scope="row"><code>Scripts</code></th><td>Add behavior when a page needs to do more than display content.</td></tr>
      </tbody></table>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section id="content-and-media" class="si-chapter" aria-labelledby="si_content_title">
    <p class="si-eyebrow">04 / CONTENT &amp; MEDIA</p>
    <h2 id="si_content_title">Give your content a home.</h2>
    <p>Keep the words, images, and supporting files close to the pages that use them. Organize your media, update your content, and build a site that has room to grow.</p>
    <div class="si-feature-pair"><article><span class="si-demo-label">CONTENT</span><h3>Write for the page.</h3><p>Edit the text in context, with the surrounding layout in view.</p></article><article><span class="si-demo-label">MEDIA</span><h3>Keep your assets together.</h3><p>Manage images and files in one place, ready for use across your site.</p></article></div>
  </section>

  <section id="styling" class="si-chapter" aria-labelledby="si_styling_title">
    <p class="si-eyebrow">05 / STYLING &amp; LAYOUT</p>
    <h2 id="si_styling_title">The small decisions make it yours.</h2>
    <p>Use visual styling controls to adjust selectors and properties. Fine-tune the space around an element, change the typography, and give your site a consistent visual language.</p>
    <div class="si-design-tokens" aria-label="This page's color palette"><span><i style="--swatch:#0b1120"></i>Canvas <code>#0b1120</code></span><span><i style="--swatch:#121d30"></i>Surface <code>#121d30</code></span><span><i style="--swatch:#7fb5ff"></i>Accent <code>#7fb5ff</code></span><span><i style="--swatch:#e8edf7"></i>Text <code>#e8edf7</code></span></div>
  </section>

  <section id="publishing" class="si-chapter" aria-labelledby="si_publishing_title">
    <p class="si-eyebrow">06 / PUBLISHING</p>
    <h2 id="si_publishing_title">A little room to get it right.</h2>
    <p>Separate the work in progress from the site your visitors see. Super Intuitive has development, test, and live stages, so you can review a change before publishing it.</p>
    <div class="si-publish-flow" aria-label="Publishing workflow"><div><span class="si-demo-label">01 / DEVELOP</span><strong>Make your changes.</strong></div><span class="si-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="si-demo-label">02 / TEST</span><strong>Check the result.</strong></div><span class="si-flow-arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div><span class="si-demo-label">03 / LIVE</span><strong>Share it with the world.</strong></div></div>
  </section>

  <section id="next-steps" class="si-chapter si-next-steps" aria-labelledby="si_next_title">
    <p class="si-eyebrow">NEXT / YOUR WEBSITE</p>
    <h2 id="si_next_title">Take it from here.</h2>
    <p>Explore the tools, learn how the pieces work, and start building something of your own.</p>
